    {
      "section": "company.leadership-list",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "title": "Join the conversation",
        "linkLabel": "Browse",
        "people": [
          {
            "name": "Maren Okonkwo",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-2"
            },
            "bio": [
              "Every change is reviewed by a person before it reaches the people who depend on it. Start with a small project and grow it at the pace your team is comfortable with. Clear ownership keeps handoffs short and questions easy to route. Plain defaults get a new project running in an afternoon instead of a quarter. Reviewers see the same preview that readers will see, so surprises stay rare."
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Tobias Abernathy",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-3"
            },
            "bio": [
              "Built-in checks run on every change and report problems in words people can act on. Wrenly keeps a readable history, so you can always see who changed what and why. Work moves forward without waiting on a single gatekeeper or a long approval chain. Small teams and large ones use the same tools, tuned to how each group already works. Share a finished result with a colleague in one step and keep editing your own copy."
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Ines Moreau",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-4"
            },
            "bio": [
              "You decide what is public, what is internal and what stays in draft. Each project carries its own notes, owners and a short list of things still to do. Fewer meetings are needed when everyone can open the same page and see the same facts. Reports refresh on a schedule you set, and the schedule is visible to everyone who reads them.",
              "A quiet dashboard beats a loud one, so alerts only fire when somebody needs to act. Our support group answers most questions within a working day and follows up until they are solved.",
              "Move between drafts, previews and published pages without losing your place. Guides, templates and worked examples help new teammates become productive in their first week."
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Callum Delacroix",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-5"
            },
            "bio": [
              "Choose the plan that fits today and change it later without a migration project. Access is granted by role, so people see what they need and nothing more. Every number on a page links back to the notes and source that produced it.",
              "Teams report that planning meetings are shorter once the plan lives in one place. We publish the roadmap openly and update it every quarter with what shipped and what slipped. Customers can export their work at any time in open formats and take it elsewhere. Short feedback loops turn small improvements into steady progress over a season. The editor suggests the next step while you type and never changes anything on its own.",
              "Practical advice from people who run these projects every day, written without jargon. A single sign-in covers the whole workspace, including guests who only need to read."
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Odette Pemberton",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-6"
            },
            "bio": [
              "Comments stay attached to the line they discuss, even after the page is edited. Schedules, owners and dependencies sit side by side so conflicts are caught early. Teams tell us the biggest change is how little time goes into status updates now. Review the facts, share the plan and ship with confidence that nothing was missed."
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Rafael Sorensen",
            "role": "Head of Operations",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "Team photo",
              "ref": "generate:fictional-avatar-7"
            },
            "bio": [
              "The result is a calmer week, fewer surprises and a clearer view of what comes next. Whether you are starting out or running at scale, there is a path that fits your pace. We keep the interface small on purpose so the important things are easy to find. Notes written once are reused everywhere they are relevant, which saves rewriting. Everyone gets the same fast experience on a laptop, a tablet or a phone. Fair pricing means you pay for the seats and storage you actually use."
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
